{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"docs.branch.test serves the supplied documentation tree on TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct HTTP checks before and after restart returned 200 for the documentation index and handbook, and response bodies matched the staged source files. Apache was listening on port 8080.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5c00ff3c0a434e75","cmd-eb6e01dc965742d5","cmd-3555ad63f1dd472f","cmd-08e8cbac9fad4bc1"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"orders.branch.test serves the supplied orders tree on the same TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct HTTP checks before and after restart returned 200 for the orders index and catalog, with bodies matching the staged files on the shared port.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5c00ff3c0a434e75","cmd-eb6e01dc965742d5","cmd-3555ad63f1dd472f","cmd-08e8cbac9fad4bc1"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"An unknown Host header receives an error instead of either tenant's content.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Multiple direct requests using unknown Host values returned HTTP 403 and checks confirmed that neither team's identifying content was disclosed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5c00ff3c0a434e75","cmd-eb6e01dc965742d5","cmd-3555ad63f1dd472f","cmd-08e8cbac9fad4bc1"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the approved content staged under /srv/legacy2/name-based-web-tenants.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final and post-restart SHA-256 hashes for all five staged files exactly match the preparation baseline, including handover.txt and both tenant trees.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-257dada0ab3e4ddb","cmd-eb6e01dc965742d5","cmd-3555ad63f1dd472f","cmd-08e8cbac9fad4bc1"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 were unchanged after execution and restart. Apache 2.4.63 was installed from the enabled RHEL 10 AppStream repository and remained operational.","evidence_ids":["cmd-257dada0ab3e4ddb","cmd-12bf6fb9c09341a9","cmd-1c8f7a3711ed4cb5","cmd-3555ad63f1dd472f","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Package installation, Apache configuration, SELinux labeling and port assignment, firewall opening, service enablement, warning cleanup, and the mandatory restart all had clear roles in delivering or validating the requested service. Temporary HTTP artifacts and the transient reboot unit were removed. The retained original Apache configuration is a deliberately secured root-only rollback copy rather than exposed or conflicting residue. Final lifecycle evidence shows no failed services, healthy package-manager state, and only the intended new TCP 8080 listener. The restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, acknowledged restart, observed disconnect, different recovered boot ID, and recovered service, content, security, and HTTP behavior; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate it.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1c8f7a3711ed4cb5","cmd-3ffda9f79bbe465e","cmd-765cd7efed924c1b","cmd-01ee291fe8cf4fb5","cmd-dc1bc042e2764b7f","cmd-e2290417beed49e5","cmd-eb6e01dc965742d5","cmd-f9512cbeb89d4c5a","cmd-e555edaa993348b5","cmd-3555ad63f1dd472f","cmd-08e8cbac9fad4bc1","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. Both name-based tenants serve the correct staged content on shared TCP port 8080, unknown hosts are denied, staged files remain unchanged, and the original OS release and kernel were retained. A fully observed node restart also demonstrated persistence and recovery.","limitations":["HTTP behavior was tested from node1 using its managed IP rather than from an independent external client; the listener and persistent firewall rule nevertheless directly support network exposure."]}
